.TH MAIL 1
.SH NAME
mail \- read mail with IMAP or POP3, send it with SMTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mail
.RB [ \-a
.IR n ]
.RB [ list
.RI [ folder ]]
.br
.B mail
.RB [ \-a
.IR n ]
.B folders
.br
.B mail
.RB [ \-a
.IR n ]
.BR read | delete
.I id
.RI [ folder ]
.br
.B mail
.RB [ \-a
.IR n ]
.B save
.I id
.RI [ folder " [" n " [" dir ]]]
.br
.B mail
.RB [ \-a
.IR n ]
.B send
.I file
.br
.B mail mailto:\fIurl\fP
.br
.B mail \-S
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mail
reads mail with IMAP or POP3 and sends it with SMTP, always over TLS. The
accounts are in
.I ~/.mail
(made by the desktop's Mail window, or by hand: see
.BR mail (5)).
Ports 993, 995 and 465 speak TLS at once; others (143, 110, 587) start
in clear and must switch to TLS (STARTTLS, STLS) before the password is
sent, or nothing is sent. IMAP keeps its connection between commands;
POP3 copies new messages into
.IR ~/Mail/INBOX ,
one file each, named by the server's UIDL.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR list " [\fIfolder\fP]"
The newest 300 messages of
.I folder
(INBOX by default): id,
.B *
if unread, date, from, subject (tab-separated). The default command.
.TP
.B folders
The folders and their unread messages (POP3: INBOX only).
.TP
.BI read " id " \fR[\fIfolder\fR]
A message as text (its text/plain part, else its HTML with the tags
stripped), and marked read.
.TP
.BI save " id " "\fR[\fIfolder \fR[\fIn \fR[\fIdir\fR]]]"
Its attachments (only the
.IR n th
with
.IR n )
into
.I ~/Downloads
(or
.IR dir ).
.TP
.BI delete " id " \fR[\fIfolder\fR]
Into the Trash; from the Trash (or with POP3), for good.
.TP
.BI send " file"
Send a draft:
.BR To: ,
.BR Cc: ,
.B Subject:
and
.B Attach:
(a file, one a line) lines, a blank line, the text. A copy goes into the
Sent folder (IMAP) unless the account says
.BR sent=0 .
.TP
.BI mailto: url
A message to the link's address (its subject, Cc and body filled in): the
text is typed, and a line with only
.B .
sends it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-a " n"
The
.IR n th
account of
.I ~/.mail
(from 0; the first by default).
.TP
.B \-S
Serve the desktop's Mail window: commands from the console, one a line,
words separated by tabs; each answer ends with a line of one 0x1e byte.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.mail
The accounts.
.TP
.I ~/Mail/INBOX
POP3's messages (another account's in
.IR ~/Mail/INBOX-N );
read ones carry the attribute
.BR seen=1 .
.TP
.I ~/Downloads
Where attachments are saved.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mail
mail read 4711
mail \-a 1 folders
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mail (5),
.BR atlas (4),
.BR fetch (1)
.SH BUGS
Messages over 8 MiB are left on the POP3 server. At most 8 accounts.
